abstract: "A vacuum-foam substrate model: noise-driven regional inflation, edge-sweeping, and near-homogeneous polarized cavities under two binding constraints (K1 vacuum discontinuity; K2 polarization-tension non-continuity). Includes the K1 critical-edge calibration (b_c = 0.1263±0.0002, corrected ratio R_edge = 1.841), the three cavity-size regimes with spectral translation, the T1 freeze-out battery, and the Companion-Bridge mapping (OQ3 closed by the W5 common-operator result). Model-level claims with executed numerical protocols; no empirical cosmological claim is made."
keywords:
  - vacuum foam
  - cavity harmonics
  - freeze-out percolation
  - critical exponents
  - companion mapping
